WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.223
In under two minutes, you will add an event to the map.

00:00:03.223 --> 00:00:04.231
We start on the map.

00:00:05.132 --> 00:00:08.522
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:10.554 --> 00:00:12.995
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:12.995 --> 00:00:15.503
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:15.503 --> 00:00:16.859
Tap Use my location.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.994
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:20.994 --> 00:00:21.678
Tap Allow.

00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:26.884
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:26.884 --> 00:00:28.008
See the three dots?

00:00:28.008 --> 00:00:28.514
Tap them.

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:31.994
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.753
Tap An event.

00:00:36.816 --> 00:00:39.911
If your event has a web page, paste it here.

00:00:39.911 --> 00:00:41.356
If not, tap No, Next.

00:00:43.132 --> 00:00:46.530
Type the event's name, and choose a season and type.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.427
Then tap Next.

00:00:51.242 --> 00:00:53.333
Pick the first and last day.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.342
Then tap Next.

00:00:56.925 --> 00:00:57.996
Free or paid?

00:00:57.996 --> 00:00:59.526
Tap Free, then Next.

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:05.443
Type the place, the city, and the street address.

00:01:05.443 --> 00:01:06.390
Then tap Next.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.972
Describe it in a sentence or two.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:13.941
Then tap Next.

00:01:18.547 --> 00:01:20.880
Check everything, and tap Add my event.

00:01:22.925 --> 00:01:25.433
Next up: Show off your house.
